 {"id":"CF-094","title":"P3 — the Tier-1 lint arm passes with a format-violating file staged whenever ruff is absent from PATH (lint.outcome=unknown, guard.passed=true), so the CF-090 tree-wide lint gate exists only on hosts that happen to have ruff","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-03T17:51:19Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T17:51:19Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"b22a64152aca10c813821c2bfbd391baba714981eabb7e1e97a7b29503877924"},"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-03 at edc8e36 (origin/main) with gitreins 0.17.1 and ruff 0.15.22 from a dedicated worktree, both arms staging the identical fixture (a Python file that ruff format --check rejects; control EXIT 1). Arm 1, ruff on PATH: guard lint outcome fail, guard.passed false, exit 1 — the arm can fail and does enforce format drift. Arm 2, PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin: lint.outcome unknown, lint.passed null, summary 'skipped — no linter on PATH', guard.passed TRUE, exit 0, with the same violating file staged, while .gitreins/config.yaml line 8 declares allow_skips: false. Nothing in the tree declares, pins or installs ruff: no requirements file, no pyproject.toml, and no code outside docs/audits mentions it. CF-090 closed the 2026-11-03 format drift and its commands reproduce at the tip (ruff check . exit 0; ruff format --check . exit 0; selftest PASS), but the gate it restored is durable only on a host that happens to carry ruff. Impact: a fresh clone, a bunker node, a CI runner or any sibling shell without ruff returns PASS on a tree-wide lint regression — the class CF-090 was filed to close — and the Tier-2 judge grades that PASS. Also observed once and not reproduced: tests/selftest.sh printed SELFTEST: FAIL (1) naming 'FAIL disk_floor — resolver missing or unreadable: <tmp>/scripts/disk_floor.py' at loadavg 37; the suite passed on the two following runs.","acceptance_criteria":"1. With a staged Python file that 'ruff format --check' rejects, running the guard on a PATH with no ruff exits non-zero and prints a named missing-linter reason. The control in docs/audits/cf094-lint-skip-arms.sh must show arm 2 with GUARD_EXIT nonzero and guard.passed: false; it currently prints GUARD_EXIT: 0 and guard.passed: true. Reverting the fix makes arm 2 pass again. 2. The linter the lint arm runs is declared by the repo (a pinned ruff version in a committed file, or a documented bootstrap the gate reads), so the gate does not depend on an unpinned host binary; the committed transcript names the ruff version used. 3. allow_skips: false in .gitreins/config.yaml governs this skip class, or the config key that does is named in docs/OPERATIONS.md with its measured behavior. 4. bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS at the fixed tip."}
 {"id":"CF-095","title":"P4 — the CF-091 census names repository tip d107ac4, but that tip carries no family-agreement check: the documented command there prints 383 rejected / 483 accepted with zero divergence lines, so the census's own totals and its one divergence class do not reproduce at the tip it cites","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-11-03T18:16:06Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T18:16:06Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"42451cf5f79f55bacc3449b85b2bdd2134bf1c020eb061223d9cfd6e1cd32a81","probe":"REPO=$HOME/code-factory; TIP=d107ac4; T=$(mktemp -d); git -C \"$REPO\" worktree add -q --detach \"$T/tip\" \"$TIP\"; grep -c family_key \"$T/tip/scripts/lane_target.py\"; sqlite3 -json \"file:$HOME/.hermes/coding-hermes/scheduler.db?mode=ro&immutable=1\" 'select name,repo_url from projects' > \"$T/projects.json\"; python3 -B \"$T/tip/scripts/lane_target.py\" repo-url --row \"$T/projects.json\" | tail -1; python3 -B \"$T/tip/scripts/lane_target.py\" repo-url --row \"$T/projects.json\" | grep -c 'diverges from primary'; git -C \"$REPO\" worktree remove --force \"$T/tip\"","source":"code-factory-review-2026-11-03-18-08-04"},"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-03 from a clean clone of origin/main (c84fc3a) and a detached worktree of the tip the artifact names. docs/audits/cf091-repo-url-census.md records 'Repository tip measured: d107ac4' with totals 866 rows / 384 rejected / 482 accepted (exit 2) and a rejection class 'repo_url diverges from primary' = 1. At that exact tip the family-agreement block is absent (grep -c family_key scripts/lane_target.py = 0) and the census's documented command, run on the same read-only export, prints '383 rejected, 483 accepted' with zero 'diverges from primary' lines. At daf2208 (the commit that adds the check) and at the tip, the same export prints 384 / 482 with exactly one divergence line, reproduced twice. The census timestamp (17:44:39Z) precedes daf2208 (17:47:02Z), so the figures came from an uncommitted working tree that became daf2208, and the artifact names the tree it did not use. Impact: CF-091's acceptance criterion 2 promises 'a later lane can diff it against a fresh run'; a lane pinning the cited tip sees a phantom one-row delta, loses the class the census highlights, and cannot tell which tree produced 384. Separately: the comparison groups only rows whose suffix is one of the nine families and exempts -sync by design (family_key returns the full lane name); 73 of the 866 exported rows end in -sync, 3 have a same-named primary, and the artifact reports no count of rows actually compared versus inspected, so its coverage is not auditable. No live divergence hides behind that exemption today: the one divergent -sync row in the export is already rejected by the per-row root check. This row is a review finding only; CF-091's enforcement claims themselves hold (selftest PASS, and disabling the block kills arms 11 and 21).","acceptance_criteria":"1. A detached worktree at the tip named in docs/audits/cf091-repo-url-census.md reproduces that artifact's totals (866 rows, 384 rejected, 482 accepted, exit 2) and prints at least one 'repo_url diverges from primary' line; today the named tip prints 383 rejected / 483 accepted and zero such lines. Name the tree that actually produced the figures (daf2208 or a later commit carrying the check) with a provenance note in docs/SCHEDULER-ADMISSION.md, or re-measure at the named tip once the check is there. CF-091's recorded tree_fp is sha256 of that census file, so a fix that edits the file must also supersede CF-091's evidence entry instead of leaving its digest stale. 2. The census states how many rows the family comparison compared versus how many it inspected (today it reports only rows inspected), so the waiver's coverage is auditable, and the number comes from the tool rather than from prose. 3. bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS at the fixed tip."}
 {"id":"CF-096","title":"P3 — ruff format --check fails at origin/main af67c3b on scripts/lane_target.py and tests/test_lane_target.py, so the tree-wide Tier-1 lint arm reds every lane judge","status":"complete","priority":"P3","complexity":1,"created_at":"2026-11-03T19:02:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T19:02:11Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"c40a67b25c6778201d034c6afc10cfe1c2f4193cb4d127a05e4ce5c9b12c1830","evidence":[{"run_id":"7c2c8c8d","ts":"2026-11-03T19:02:11Z","tree_fp":"69aca079858ea0fd2452c08a190903f67412d9e6634a8b3e5fc937ed83975cc2","artifacts":["docs/audits/cf096-ruff-drift-transcript.txt"]}]},"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-03 by the readme lane at origin/main af67c3b with ruff 0.15.22: a pristine git archive export of that commit fails ruff format --check on exactly those two files (2 files would be reformatted, 9 already formatted, rc 1), so the GitReins lint arm — which scans the tree, not the diff — fails for every lane regardless of what that lane changed. CF-090 closed the same class on 2026-11-03 and its commands reproduce; this is a fresh drift introduced by af67c3b (docs: document bunker:// targets), not a regression of the closed row, and not CF-094 (which is the arm SKIPPING when ruff is absent). Because a red lint arm makes every verdict instrument-fail, the readme lane paid it down in the same tick rather than leaving it for the next one: ruff format on the two files, formatting only (ruff format --diff shows argument and flag wrapping; the judge independently compared ast.dump between af67c3b and the fixed commit and found identical ASTs).","acceptance_criteria":"1. At origin/main af67c3b (pristine export) ruff format --check . exits 1 naming exactly scripts/lane_target.py and tests/test_lane_target.py. 2. After the fix ruff check . and ruff format --check . both exit 0, python3 -B tests/test_lane_target.py exits 0, and bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS at the fixed tip. 3. The change is formatting only: ruff format --diff shows wrapping and no statement change.","commit_hash":"2f24e54","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"SKIP","worker_summary":"ruff format on scripts/lane_target.py + tests/test_lane_target.py; tree-wide lint arm green again (ruff check + format --check exit 0, selftest PASS); judge PASS bound to 61db6f7 which contains this commit"}
+{"id":"CF-097","title":"P4 \u2014 the CF-085 repo-url guard dropped the workdir arm's not_home_repo check: verify rejects a checkout whose git top level is $HOME (exit 4) while repo-url accepts the same path (exit 0), so a project row pointed at the home meta-repo \u2014 the census's largest rejection class \u2014 passes the new guard","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":1,"created_at":"2026-11-03T19:10:52Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T19:10:52Z","detail":{},"reasoning":"scripts/lane_target.py has two arms that probe the same kind of root and disagree about what a valid root is. The older workdir arm (verify/scan) applies not_home_repo ('the stand-in defect: a workdir inside $HOME whose git top level IS $HOME') and fails the path with exit 4. The repo-url arm added by CF-085 reuses _local_checkout and compares the top level with the path, but never applies not_home_repo, so the same checkout passes with exit 0. Measured 2026-11-03 at origin/main 780a1e2 with a hermetic fixture (HOME set to the fixture root, so the result does not depend on the host's real home): verify exit 4 with {\"check\":\"not_home_repo\",\"ok\":false,\"value\":\"top level is the home directory\"}; repo-url exit 0 printing PASS repo_url 'local:<fixture>' \u2014 root '<fixture>' HEAD <sha>. The live consequence is the class the guard was built for: the CF-091 census's largest rejection class is 253 stand-in roots whose git top level resolves to the home meta-repo, and a scheduler row whose repo_url is the home meta-repo itself (rather than a path inside it) is accepted while every consumer of a repo_url treats that root as non-evidence. No live scheduler row currently carries the bare home root (measured 0 of 866 in docs/audits/cf091-repo-url-census.json's live export), so this is a latent fail-open rather than a live break; it is filed because the arm it was copied from applies the check and the same file calls that root the stand-in defect. Distinct from CF-053 (repoints lane workdirs, not repo_url), CF-060 (a checkout of a different repository), CF-062 (scan --allow-remote) and CF-095 (census provenance).","acceptance_criteria":"0. Reproduce on the current tree: run the probe from the repo root; it prints verify_rc=4 with a not_home_repo check whose ok is false, and repo_url_rc=0 PASS for the same path under the same HOME. 1. repo-url rejects a local root whose realpath is the home directory (the same $HOME the verify arm resolves) with a named reason and exit 4, naming the home-directory condition rather than reporting a generic failure. 2. tests/test_lane_target.py proves both arms hermetically with HOME set inside the fixture: the home-rooted repo is rejected by repo-url as well as by verify, and a non-home real git root is still accepted; no test may depend on the host's real HOME. 3. tests/selftest.sh gains an arm for that rejection which goes RED against the pre-fix lane_target.py, naming the missing check rather than a generic nonzero exit. 4. bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS and scripts/boardctl validate prints RESULT: OK.","probe":"d=$(mktemp -d); git init -q -b main \"$d/h\"; git -C \"$d/h\" -c user.email=f@example.invalid -c user.name=f commit -q --allow-empty -m fixture; vout=$(HOME=\"$d/h\" python3 -B scripts/lane_target.py verify \"$d/h\" 2>&1); vrc=$?; rout=$(HOME=\"$d/h\" python3 -B scripts/lane_target.py repo-url \"local:$d/h\" 2>&1); rrc=$?; echo \"verify_rc=$vrc $(printf '%s' \"$vout\" | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(json.dumps([c for c in d[\"checks\"] if c[\"check\"]==\"not_home_repo\"]))')\"; echo \"repo_url_rc=$rrc $(printf '%s' \"$rout\" | head -1)\""}
+{"id":"CF-098","title":"P4 \u2014 a 200-line code commit can land untraced and unguarded: af67c3b changed scripts/lane_target.py and tests/ under a 'docs:' subject with no board row, no ch:trace and no verdict, and its ruff-format drift is the only untraced code commit on main since 3b2c81e","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-11-03T19:10:52Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T19:10:52Z","detail":{},"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-03 at origin/main 780a1e2. Enumerating every commit in 3b2c81e..HEAD that touches scripts/, tests/ or specs/ and whose message carries no ch:trace yields exactly one: af67c3b ('docs: document bunker:// targets and how they are proved on the agent'), which added 142 lines to scripts/lane_target.py, 68 to tests/test_lane_target.py and 2 to specs/NODE.md. That commit has no board row (the bunker rows on the board are CF-009/CF-041/CF-052/CF-053/CF-056/CF-057/CF-063/CF-072/CF-075, none describing verify_bunker or the plan subcommand) and no verdict naming it (git grep af67c3b under .gitreins/ = 0 hits). Its staged file is refused by the guard today: in a clean clone of af67c3b with the canonical scripts/lane_target.py staged, gitreins guard --json returns lint outcome=fail ('ruff format --check: 1 file(s) would be reformatted'), guard.passed=false, exit 1 \u2014 so the commit did not pass the guard, it bypassed it undisclosed, and because grep -c ruff tests/selftest.sh = 0 there is no repo-side arm that would catch the drift afterwards either. The cost was concrete: the tree stayed red on the CF-090 lint criterion until a sibling lane filed and fixed it as CF-096. This row tracks the governance gap (an untraced code commit plus an undisclosed bypass), not the formatting, which CF-096 already fixed.","acceptance_criteria":"0. Reproduce on the current tree: run the probe from the repo root; it prints exactly one untraced line naming af67c3b and an untraced_total=1 count over 3b2c81e..HEAD. 1. af67c3b carries a board disposition: a follow-up commit that names it with a ch:trace marker binding it to a row id, or a committed audit note under docs/audits/ stating why a code change landed under a docs: subject with no row. 2. A gate fails on the class rather than on this instance: a committed check refuses a commit whose staged paths include scripts/, tests/ or specs/ while its message carries no ch:trace marker (or carries a docs:-only subject), and a RED proof in the tree shows a fixture commit without the trailer being refused. 3. The check does not fire on board-only or docs-only commits, and the control arm passes for a commit that carries the trailer. 4. bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS and scripts/boardctl validate prints RESULT: OK.","probe":"n=0; for c in $(git rev-list 3b2c81e..HEAD); do if git show --stat --format= $c | grep -qE '^ (scripts|tests|specs)/'; then if ! git log -1 --format=%B $c | grep -q 'ch:trace'; then n=$((n+1)); echo \"untraced $(git log -1 --format='%h %s' $c)\"; fi; fi; done; echo \"untraced_total=$n\""}
